#HELP_BEGIN
FILENAME: Inogeni TOGGLE ROOMS / XT
MANUFACTURER: Inogeni
MODEL: TOGGLE ROOMS / XT

CATEGORY: Video/USB Selector
VERSION: 2

SUMMARY: Provides RS232, Telnet Or REST API control for device commands

TOGGLE ROOMS Telnet server auto close connection when it does not receive communication for 10 sec.
It is normal to see Telnet connection going down when Polling is disabled.


SETUP OF CRESTRON HARDWARE:
BAUD RATE - 9600
PARITY - NONE
DATA BITS - 8
STOP BITS - 1

VENDOR FIRMWARE: v1.21

******************************************************************
PARAMETERS:

NAME              TYPE DESCRIPTION

Control            P   Select RS232, Telnet Or REST API control.
                   

******************************************************************
INPUT DESCRIPTIONS:

NAME                  TYPE DESCRIPTION  


Module_Enable         D    Enable module and start communication with the device.
Reboot                D    Reboot the device
FactoryDefault        D    Erase the current configuration onboard and return to default values.
Version               D    Pulse to get Firmware version
Status                D    Pulse to get current device status
USBC4K60EN            D    Pulse to Toggle USB-C support 4K60, no effect when using 4K60 and up Fixed EDID
DisplayScaler         D    Pulse to Toggle down scaling of Display output, all inputs scale to 1080p
ShareScaler           D    Pulse to Toggle down scaling of Share output, all inputs scale to 1080p
DisplayCECPowerOn     D    Pulse to send CEC Power ON command.
DisplayCECPowerOff    D    Pulse to send CEC Power OFF command.
CECPassthrough         D    Pulse to Toggle, CEC passthrough allows CEC controls from the selected HDMI input to the Display.
AutoHDMIcecPower      D    Pulse to Toggle, Auto Power ON / Off based on HDMI video presence. (Disable CECpassthrough if not working as expected.)

POLL                  D    Set high/1 to enable polling. Returns the current view of the device, firmware version and inputs resolutions.
debug                 D    Set high/1 to enable debug print
 
HostMeeting           A    Change value to change Host Meeting (Video and USB to same Host)
HostMeetingPriority   A    Change value to set a preferred Host, default 3 (last connected)
DisplaySource         A    Change value to set Display out source.
ShareSource           A    Change value to set Share out source.
USB_Host              A    Change value to set USB Host source

OperationMode         A    Change value to set Operation Mode, default 0 (BYOD with content sharing)

//Only valid in Custom Mode (Operation Mode 2)
USBSwitchMode         A    Change value to set desired Mode
USBPriority           A    Change value to set desired Priority
DisplaySwitchMode     A    Change value to set desired Mode
DisplayPriority       A    Change value to set desired Priority
ShareSwitchMode       A    Change value to set desired Mode
SharePriority         A    Change value to set desired Priority

USBDevicePower_RoomPC A    Change value to control USB Ports Power in RoomPC Host
USBDevicePower_LUSBc  A    Change value to control USB Ports Power in Laptop USB-C Host
USBDevicePower_LHdmi  A    Change value to control USB Ports Power in Laptop HDMI Host
USBDevicePower_Nohost A    Change value to control USB Ports Power in No Host

Rx$                   S    Serial data string to be routed from a COM port.


******************************************************************
OUTPUT DESCRIPTIONS:

NAME                  TYPE DESCRIPTION

TelnetConnected_fb    D    High when Telnet is connected only with IP control.
USBC4K60EN_fb         D    HIGH when USB-C support 4K60
CECPassthrough_fb      D    HIGH when CEC Passthrough is enabled 
AutoHDMIcecPower_fb   D    HIGH when Auto CEC controls is enabled.
DisplayScaler_fb      D    HIGH when Display out is scaled to 1080p
ShareScaler_fb        D    HIGH when Share out is scaled to 1080p

TelnetSocketStatus_fb A    Current value of Crestron TCP client
DisplaySource_fb      A    Current value of Display out source
ShareSource_fb        A    Current value of Share out source
USB_Host_fb           A    Current value of USB Host source
HostMeetingPriority_fb A   Current value of Host Meeting Priority

OperationMode_fb      A   Current value of Operation Mode

USBSwitchMode_fb      A   Current value of USB switching mode
USBPriority_fb        A   Current value of USB Host Priority
DisplaySwitchMode_fb  A   Current value of Display out switch mode
DisplayPriority_fb    A   Current value of Display out Priority
ShareSwitchMode_fb    A   Current value of Share out switch mode
SharePriority_fb      A   Current value of Share out Priority

USBDevicePower_RoomPC_fb A    Current value of USB Ports Power in RoomPC Host
USBDevicePower_LUSBc_fb  A    Current value of USB Ports Power in Laptop USB-C Host
USBDevicePower_LHdmi_fb  A    Current value of USB Ports Power in Laptop HDMI Host
USBDevicePower_Nohost_fb A    Current value of USB Ports Power in No Host
                   
FirmV                 S    Report Firmware version
IP_Address            S    Report IP Address
IP_SubnetMask         S    Report SubnetMask
IP_Gateway            S    Report Gateway
MAC_Address           S    Report MAC Address

HostMeeting_fb        S    Report String of current Host Meeting, based on USB Host value and Display out value. 

USBC_Video_fb         S    Report Detected Laptop USB-C video formats
Laptop_Video_fb       S    Report Detected Laptop HDMI video formats
RoomPC_Video_fb       S    Report Detected RoomPC video formats             

Tx$                   S    Serial data string to be routed to a COM port.
#HELP_END

